  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Prioritize personal safety first, document the damage, prevent further water entry, and contact your insurance provider and a reputable roofing contractor.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "document the damage, prevent further water entry, and contact your insurance provider and a reputable roofing contractor"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "1. Check Safety First"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Stay off the roof, especially when wet or structurally compromised ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Watch for downed power lines, gas smells, or exposed electrical wiring; evacuate and call emergency or utility services if you spot hazards."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Turn off power at the breaker box if water leaks near outlets or fixtures."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Look indoors for sagging ceilings, bulging walls, or active leaks, and leave immediately if the structure feels unsafe .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "2. Document Everything"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Take timestamped photos and videos of roof damage, fallen debris, detached flashing, and interior leaks before making temporary fixes ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Save local weather alerts, hail reports, or storm warnings to verify when the damage occurred."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Keep receipts for emergency supplies, tarps, and temporary repairs.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              3,
              4,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "3. Mitigate Further Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Place buckets under active indoor leaks and move valuables out of the way."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cover exposed roof decking or holes with a heavy-duty tarp or plastic sheeting anchored over the ridge line."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Safely clear light debris or branches if reachable from the ground, but leave heavy trees or roof access to professionals.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3,
              5,
              6
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "4. Contact Insurance and Contractors"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Notify your homeowners insurance company promptly and ask about coverage, deductibles, and adjuster scheduling."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Schedule an inspection with a licensed, local roofing contractor."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Avoid high-pressure \"storm-chasing\" contractors who knock on doors immediately after bad weather.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              3,
              4,
              5,
              6,
              7
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Homeowners and roofing specialists emphasize putting safety ahead of property, acting quickly on documentation and mitigation, and vetting contractors carefully after severe weather."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For more guidance on rebuilding after severe storms, see Quora, or review post-storm steps at State Roofing.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Quora",
            "link": "https://www.quora.com/How-can-I-rebuild-a-roof-that-was-ruined-by-a-storm"
          },
          {
            "text": "State Roofing",
            "link": "https://www.stateroofing.com/blog/what-should-i-do-right-after-storm-damage/"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          4,
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you share the type of storm (such as wind, hail, or heavy snow), your roofing material, and whether there is active leaking, I can give more specific next steps."
      }
